(Bug #69 over a map. A map's values are runtime-tagged the way a mixed
 list's slots are (LANGUAGE.md:2409-2411), so a `value` in the clause has a
 tag on both sides of the comparison here too.)

a map called person is {"name": "Ada", "age": 36}.

a value called probe is "Ada".
print each detail from person's values treating probe as "Grace".

a value called age is 36.
print each detail from person's values treating age as 37.
